{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.SymmetricCoxeter","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SytRowSuperstandard","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.BruhatRankCriterion"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.dominance_iff_bruhatLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.dominance_iff_bruhatLe","kind":"theorem","line":686,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L686-L700","doc":"**Dipper–James 3.7**, assembled from its two halves.\n\nThis declaration itself contains **no `sorry`** — it is the conjunction of\n`dominance_to_bruhatLe` and `bruhatLe_to_dominance`, and inherits exactly their status.\n**The converse half is proved; the forward half is not**, so a consumer that needs only\n`d(s) ≤ d(t) → s ⊵ t` should cite `bruhatLe_to_dominance` directly rather than this `iff`,\nwhich is `sorry`-carrying through its other half.  See each half's own docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.bruhatLe_to_dominance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.bruhatLe_to_dominance","kind":"theorem","line":651,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L651-L684","doc":"**The converse half of 3.7 — PROVED, and it never needed `qou-3k66`.**\n\nMathas' own argument for this direction goes through the *reflection* order (`d(t) = d(s)·τ`\nwith `ℓ` up by one), which is why the corpus recorded it as blocked on **`BruhatLe → ReflLe`**\n— bean `qou-3k66`, whose own summary names it as *\"what a consumer citing Mathas' Prop 3.7\nneeds for an `↔`\"*.  **That route is not the only one.**  The chain used here is\n\n    d(s) ≤ d(t)  →  rank inequality      (`BruhatRank.rk_le_of_bruhatLe`, the EASY half of\n                                          Ehresmann's criterion, proved straight from the\n                                          SUBWORD definition — no reflection order at all)\n                 →  at the row cuts      (specialisation, `rankAt_eq_rk`)\n                 →  s ⊵ t                (`domRel_iff_rankAt`)\n\nso 3.7 was never a reason to prioritise `qou-3k66`.  A sibling has since closed that bean\nindependently; this route did not use it either way.\n\n**The row-standardness hypotheses are not used**, and that is a real observation rather than\nan oversight: `domRel` is a relation on *tabloids* and `dOf` is a bijection on *all*\ntableaux, so this implication holds for arbitrary `μ`-tableaux.  They are kept in the\nsignature because 3.7 as stated in the source quantifies over row-standard tableaux and the\nforward half does need them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.dominance_to_bruhatLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.dominance_to_bruhatLe","kind":"theorem","line":605,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L605-L649","doc":"**Dipper–James (Mathas 3.7): dominance on row-standard tableaux is the Bruhat order.**\n\n**The forward half of 3.7** — dominance implies Bruhat.\n\n`domRel a b` reads \"`a` is dominated by `b`\", so `domRel ⟦t⟧ ⟦s⟧` is \"`s` dominates `t`\".\nThe Bruhat side is `d(s) ≤ d(t)` — **reversing**; see the module docstring, and\n`refTab_dOf_bruhatLe` for the fact that forces it.\n\n**PROVED, unconditionally.**  A two-line composition — `domRel_iff_rankAt` turns dominance\ninto a rank comparison at the row cuts, `rk_le_of_rankAt_le` interpolates it to every index —\napplied to `BruhatRank.bruhatLe_of_rk_le`, the **hard direction of Ehresmann's criterion**,\nwhich is itself now proved sorry-free (induction on `ℓ(w)` at a right descent).\n\n`#print axioms` gives `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]` — **no `sorryAx`**.  Note that\nis the honest check: a file with no `sorry` token can still depend on one, and this\ndeclaration did until the Ehresmann half landed.\n\nMathas' own route is not what closed it.  His tableau induction measures **78.8 %** on its\n`s ⊵ v` clause (see the module docstring); the route taken here has no tableau content in it\nat all.\n\nMathas' own route needed a correct selection rule for the inductive step's transposition; one\nexists (some transposition works for **every** pair, 142 314/142 314) but none of seven tried\nfinds it, and the negative results say no rule naming a label can. That route is abandoned in\nfavour of this one, and `qou-f3mc` records why.\n\nNote that `_ht` is unused: `rk_le_of_rankAt_le` needs row-standardness only of the\n*dominating* tableau `s`.\n\nThe **statement** is not in doubt: measured exhaustively over every ordered pair of\nrow-standard tableaux of every partition of `n ≤ 6`, **708 062/708 062**, under both\ndefinitions of the Bruhat order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.rk_le_of_rankAt_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.rk_le_of_rankAt_le","kind":"theorem","line":569,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L569-L601","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.exists_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.exists_block","kind":"theorem","line":555,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L555-L567","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.rowPrefix_colLen_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.rowPrefix_colLen_zero","kind":"theorem","line":551,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L551-L553","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.dOf_increasingOn_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.dOf_increasingOn_block","kind":"theorem","line":509,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L509-L536","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.colPattern_refTab_eq_of_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.colPattern_refTab_eq_of_block","kind":"theorem","line":501,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L501-L507","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.rowPattern_refTab_eq_of_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.rowPattern_refTab_eq_of_block","kind":"theorem","line":488,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L488-L499","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.colPattern_refTab_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.colPattern_refTab_lt","kind":"theorem","line":482,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L482-L486","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.refTab_val_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.refTab_val_eq","kind":"theorem","line":470,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L470-L480","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.colPattern_dOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.colPattern_dOf","kind":"theorem","line":466,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L466-L468","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.rankAt_eq_rk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.rankAt_eq_rk","kind":"theorem","line":432,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L432-L449","doc":"**`rankAt` IS `BruhatRank.rk`**, at the cut `rowPrefix μ (i + 1)` and after the\nvalue-preserving relabelling `toFinSucc`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.rowPattern_refTab_le_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.rowPattern_refTab_le_iff","kind":"theorem","line":398,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L398-L430","doc":"**The row cut is an initial segment.**  `refTab` is row-superstandard, so a label lies\nin row `≤ i` exactly when it is below the cumulative row length `rowPrefix μ (i + 1)`.\n\nThis is the fact `rankAt` was deliberately stated *without*, so that everything up to here\nstayed independent of the reference tableau's shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.domRel_iff_rankAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.domRel_iff_rankAt","kind":"theorem","line":372,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L372-L388","doc":"**Dominance restated with no tableaux in it**: `s ⊵ t` is exactly the rank inequality\nbetween `d(s)` and `d(t)`, read at the reference tableau's row cuts.\n\nThis is the left-hand column of 3.7.  The right-hand column — the Bruhat order — is the\n*same* inequality read at **every** index rather than only at the row cuts (Ehresmann's\ncriterion), and the two are reconciled by `d` being a minimal coset representative.  See the\nmodule docstring for the measurement and for what each half of 3.7 then needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.domCount_eq_rankAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.domCount_eq_rankAt","kind":"theorem","line":361,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L361-L370","doc":"**The dominance count IS the rank matrix.**  Reindexing the `domCount` filter along the\nbijection `dOf t` and applying `rowPattern_dOf`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.rankAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.rankAt","kind":"def","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L350-L359","doc":"**The rank matrix of `d(t)`**, cut by the reference tableau's rows: the number of labels\n`x` that `refTab` puts in row `≤ i` and `d(t)` sends below `m`.\n\nStated against `rowPattern (refTab μ) x ≤ i` rather than against a numeric row boundary\n`x < μ₀ + ⋯ + μ_i`.  The two agree — `refTab` is row-superstandard — but that equality is a\nseparate fact about the reference tableau, and nothing below needs it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.rowPattern_dOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.rowPattern_dOf","kind":"theorem","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L337-L348","doc":"**The key identity**: `d(t)` transports `t`'s row pattern back to the *reference*\ntableau's.\n\n`dOf t x = t⁻¹(refTab x)`, so `t` sends `dOf t x` to the cell `refTab` assigns to `x`, and\nthe row of that cell does not mention `t` at all.  Two lines, and it is the reason 3.7 has\nno tableau content: the row of a label in `t` is the row of its `d(t)`-preimage in the\nreference tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.refTab_dOf_bruhatLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceIsBruhat.refTab_dOf_bruhatLe","kind":"theorem","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DominanceIsBruhat.lean#L316-L330","doc":"**The reference tableau maps to the bottom of the Bruhat order.**\n\nSorry-free, and it pins the orientation of `dominance_iff_bruhatLe` below: `refTab` is\ndominance-maximal, so under 3.7 it must be Bruhat-*minimal*, which is exactly what this says.\nAnyone tempted to state 3.7 the other way round should read this first. ","signatureChunk":0}]}